From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 08:33:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 172/181] fix(gastown): run each polecat gate as one foreground
 call, not a background poll (gcp-ypugs)

A polecat spent 17-25 model calls on each gate step (preflight 18.7-24.7,
self-review 16.8-18.2) for a step whose real work is one command, because the
model chose run_in_background for the gate and then polled it. Each poll
re-reads 70-100K tokens of context. The pack text never asked for
backgrounding: Claude Code caps a foreground Bash call at 10 minutes, and gate
steps often run longer (winnow self-review p50 10.0m, gascity-packs 21.4m), so
a foreground gate was impossible.

The polecat agent now sets env BASH_MAX_TIMEOUT_MS=3600000, which raises the
cap only. The default stays at 120s, so an ordinary hung command still times
out. Each gate stub in mol-polecat-work (preflight-tests and self-review) gets
a four-line paragraph that asks for a FOREGROUND call with the Bash timeout
parameter set to 3600000, no run_in_background and no polling. The stubs, the
gate commands, polecat-gates.sh, the receipts and the refinery are unchanged.

Two tests in test_polecat_gates.sh pin it: each gate step holds the paragraph
once, directly before the stub fence, and the agent env equals the number in
that paragraph and leaves BASH_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS unset, so the two cannot
drift apart. Both were seen failing against a broken edit before this commit.

Not measured here: the per-gate call-count drop, which is a seat check after
the city pin includes this change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 gastown/agents/polecat/agent.toml      |  5 +++
 gastown/formulas/mol-polecat-work.toml | 11 ++++++
 gastown/tests/test_polecat_gates.sh    | 53 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 69 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gastown/agents/polecat/agent.toml b/gastown/agents/polecat/agent.toml
index 0374c366..86f88a03 100644
--- a/gastown/agents/polecat/agent.toml
+++ b/gastown/agents/polecat/agent.toml
@@ -8,5 +8,10 @@ pre_start = ["{{.ConfigDir}}/assets/scripts/worktree-setup.sh {{.RigRoot}} {{.Wo
 # ../../README.md ("Default Sling Formula").
 default_sling_formula = "mol-polecat-work"
 idle_timeout = "2h"
+# Claude Code caps a foreground Bash call at 10 minutes unless this is raised,
+# and a gate step often runs longer, so the model backgrounded the gate and
+# polled it (gcp-ypugs). mol-polecat-work asks for a 3600000 ms foreground call
+# on its gate stubs; keep the two numbers equal.
+env = { BASH_MAX_TIMEOUT_MS = "3600000" }
 min_active_sessions = 0
 max_active_sessions = 5
diff --git a/gastown/formulas/mol-polecat-work.toml b/gastown/formulas/mol-polecat-work.toml
index 95a3942d..d49b019e 100644
--- a/gastown/formulas/mol-polecat-work.toml
+++ b/gastown/formulas/mol-polecat-work.toml
@@ -595,6 +595,11 @@ red is never filed under any other name, because the skip keys on the name: a
 pytest red filed as `phase=test` would silently skip `go test` on a rig whose
 test_command is `go test` (gcp-98gh).
 
+Run it in the FOREGROUND, with the Bash tool's timeout parameter set to 3600000
+(60 minutes). Do not set run_in_background and do not poll: the call returns
+when every gate has finished, with the verdict. A gate prints nothing until it
+ends, so a quiet wait is normal.
