 ```bash
 PG_SRC=$(gc formula list --json 2>/dev/null | jq -r '.formulas[]? | select(.name == "mol-polecat-work") | .source // empty' | head -1)
 PG="${PG_SRC:+$(dirname "$(dirname "$PG_SRC")")/assets/scripts/polecat-gates.sh}"
@@ -691,6 +696,12 @@ shell: every check and the test run append to the same gate log, which
 `known-red` reads in §3. Tests are the rig's `affected_tests_command` when it
 sets one, else its `test_command` as configured (which may itself select by
 diff). Each phase is named after the formula var that holds its command.
+
+Run it in the FOREGROUND, with the Bash tool's timeout parameter set to 3600000
+(60 minutes). Do not set run_in_background and do not poll: the call returns
+when every gate has finished, with the verdict. A gate prints nothing until it
+ends, so a quiet wait is normal.
+
 ```bash
 : "${BASE_REF:?base ref not resolved — run step 1 of this step first}"
